Q9. Explain how an RDBMS uses tables, rows, and columns to organize data.
An RDBMS (Relational Database Management System) organizes data into tables
consisting of rows and columns, making it easy to store, retrieve, and manage
information.


Q10. Describe two advantages and two limitations of using an RDBMS.
1. Advantages of RDBMS
1. Data Accuracy and Integrity
• RDBMS maintains accurate and consistent data using primary keys, foreign keys,
and constraints.
• It helps prevent duplicate records and invalid relationships.
2. Data Security
• RDBMS provides security features to protect sensitive information.
• It allows administrators to control who can access, modify, or delete data.
2. Limitations of RDBMS
1. High Cost
• Some RDBMS solutions require expensive software licenses, hardware, and
maintenance.
• Skilled database administrators may be needed.
2. Complexity
• Designing and managing relational databases can be complicated.
• Large databases may require performance optimization and regular
maintenance.
